-- title:
--   Twisted hyperbolic slope and intercept as twisted orbital class sums
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields which is Galois and finite-dimensional, with $\sigma$ an element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every automorphism lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$, and with $[L:K]$ prime. Fix reals $0<\alpha<\beta$; fundamental domains $\Phi_L$, $\Phi_K$ for the global points of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ inside the idele-norm window $\mathrm{Icc}\,\alpha\,\beta$ for the restricted adelic Haar measures, fundamental domains $\Omega_L$, $\Omega_K$ for the principal ideles inside the idele units for Haar measures $\nu_{Z_L}$, $\nu_{Z_K}$, a Galois descent datum $D$ for the ideles of $L$, finite sets of finite places $S_K$ of $K$ and $S_L$ of $L$ satisfying the stated compatibilities (all places above $S_K$ lie in $S_L$, $S_L$ is a union of fibres, ramification indices are $1$ above places outside $S_K$), a character $\xi_L$ of the idele units of $L$ that is continuous, trivial on principal ideles and takes equal values on determinants of the Hecke generators at places in a common fibre outside $S_L$, levels $N$, $N'$ supported in $S_L$, $S_K$, archimedean type families, local and archimedean test components, a compact set $X$ containing the set of Hecke parameters cut out by the displayed Ramanujan-type bounds and normalisations, a finite set $\Xi$ of characters of the idele units of $K$ characterised by continuity, triviality on principal ideles and by pulling back to $\xi_L$ along the idelic norm, a constant $c_0$, and the hypothesis `hgeo` that for every finite set of places containing $S_K$ the $\xi_L$-folded elliptic-plus-central twisted kernel integral over $\Phi_L\times\Omega_L$ equals $c_0$ times the sum over $\Xi$ of the corresponding $\xi_K$-folded central-plus-elliptic kernel integrals over $\Phi_K\times\Omega_K$. Then, for every finite set $T$ of places of $K$ disjoint from $S_K$ with at least two elements and with all places above $T$ outside $S_L$, for all choices of extensions $w_v$ of the places of $T$ to $L$, of the places $w'$, of uniformisers $\varpi_v$ upstairs and $\varpi_{K,v}$ downstairs, of Hecke coset systems $r_{T}$, $r_K$ for the corresponding integral subgroups and of the central elements $z$, $z_K$, for all exponent functions $k$, $j$, for every continuous compactly supported $\varphi_L$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ admitting the displayed semi-local factorisation whose components at the places of $T$ are the indicated sums of translates of the semi-local integral-set indicator by products of Hecke representatives, bi-invariant under $\mathrm{levelOne}(N)$ intersected with the finite-adelic subgroup and archimedeanly bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$, for every family $\mathrm{fam}$ indexed by the slot indices with the listed invariance, archimedean finiteness and factorisation properties, and matching $\varphi_L$ at $S_K\cup T$ against the slot-coefficient combination of the $\mathrm{fam}$, and for all complex $A$, $B$ and real $R_0$ such that for every $R\ge R_0$ the $\xi_L$-folded integral over the canonical truncation domain of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted hyperbolic class sum minus the indicated truncated constant term equals $R\cdot A+B$: given in addition the closed subgroup $H$ of diagonal adelic matrices whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twist differs from themselves by a central element, with right-invariant Haar measure $\mu_H$, the group $\Lambda_0$ of diagonal rational matrices with norm-ratio in $K$, a constant $\kappa_0>0$ and a fundamental domain $\Omega$ realising the two displayed exact volume formulas $\kappa_0|2R-\log\mathrm{ht}(y)-\log\mathrm{ht}(wy)|$, a set $\Delta$ of diagonal rational matrices of norm-ratio $\neq 1$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-conjugacy saturations are pairwise disjoint and cover the hyperbolic norm classes, the $\sigma^{-1}$-invariance of $\xi_L$ under $D$, a Haar measure $\mu$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K)$ and positive constants $c_\mu,c_H,c_\tau,c_N$ together with the stated measure-comparison identities for base change, for $H$, for the twisted centralisers, for the subgroup $A_K$ of base-changed ideles and for the norm-one subgroup $N_1=\ker(\text{idelic norm})$ with its Haar-quotient formula, a lift $\delta$ of $\Delta$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K)$, Haar measures $\tau(t)$ on the twisted centralisers, and functions $I_L$, $J_L$ realising, for each $t\in\Delta$ and each idele $w$, the twisted orbital integral and the twisted weighted orbital integral (with weight $-\log\mathrm{ht}(x)-\log\mathrm{ht}(wx)$) of the $w$-translate of $\varphi_L$ pulled back along base change: there exists a finite subset $\Delta_\varphi\subseteq\Delta$ such that for every finite $S$ with $\Delta_\varphi\subseteq S\subseteq\Delta$ the functions $\xi_L\cdot I_L(t,\cdot)$ and $\xi_L\cdot J_L(t,\cdot)$ are integrable on the $N_1$-orbit quotient of the idele units for the Haar quotient measure, and $A=\sum_{t\in S}2\kappa_0\varepsilon_t\,(c_Nc_\tau/(c_Hc_\mu))\int \xi_L\,I_L(t)$ while $B=\sum_{t\in S}\kappa_0\varepsilon_t\,(c_Nc_\tau/(c_Hc_\mu))\int \xi_L\,J_L(t)$, where $\varepsilon_t=1/2$ if $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11})=-1$ and $\varepsilon_t=1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the hyperbolic contribution to the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for cyclic base change on $\mathrm{GL}(2)$, as in Langlands's treatment: the linear growth in the truncation height is carried by the plain twisted orbital integrals and the constant term by the weighted ones. In contrast with the textbook account, the statement is entirely conditional and bookkeeping-explicit: the affine behaviour in $R$ of the truncated twisted hyperbolic term, all fundamental domains, Haar normalisations, unfolding constants $c_\mu,c_H,c_\tau,c_N$, the volume constant $\kappa_0$, the class family $\Delta$ with its lift $\delta$ and twisted-centraliser measures, and the realisation of $I_L$, $J_L$ as twisted and weighted twisted orbital integrals are supplied as hypotheses, and the conclusion only identifies the slope $A$ and intercept $B$ as finite class sums over any sufficiently large finite $S\subseteq\Delta$. It feeds the comparison of the hyperbolic slope upstairs with the slot-coefficient combination downstairs, and from there the winding-datum form of the intercept identity on $K$.
